task: intent-distil-diversity
agent: fable-persist
started: 2026-09-07
branch: feature/intent-distil-diversity
worktree: ../okay-wt-div

why: the entry says the distilled corpus's distribution is narrow
  rather than its labels wrong, and that "measuring the corpus's own
  diversity (say, distinct trigram ratio against the human fixture's)
  is the honest way to tell whether it worked". The measurement half
  needs no teacher and gives any later corpus — generated any way — a
  number to beat before it is embedded.

what: TestDistilDiversity (offline, in the gate): distinct-1/2/3
  ratios, vocabulary size, words per message, and distinct openers
  per message, for the human fixture against the distilled corpus
  (all, and the self-consistent 182), on SAMPLES OF EQUAL SIZE (the
  ratios are length-sensitive) averaged over twenty seeded draws;
  per class; the shared-vocabulary share; the commonest openers on
  each side. The persona/register prompting half is filed with the
  number it would have to move, not built: more generation is what
  intent-distil-dose and intent-distil-static just measured as one
  split's gain and no gain.
